\title{glycoPathDesign: measurement design for glycoform pathway inference}
\description{
\code{glycoPathDesign} asks whether a proposed site-specific glycoform panel can
distinguish the effective reaction-rate classes specified by a biosynthetic
pathway model, and what assay precision that distinction requires.
}
\details{
The main workflow is:
\enumerate{
\item Define a pathway with \code{\link[=glyco_pathway]{glyco_pathway()}}.
\item Inspect its forward prediction with \code{\link[=predict_composition]{predict_composition()}}.
\item Audit a proposed panel with \code{\link[=check_panel]{check_panel()}}.
\item Test operating-point robustness with \code{\link[=check_operating_points]{check_operating_points()}}.
\item Search alternatives with \code{\link[=enumerate_panels]{enumerate_panels()}} and \code{\link[=optimise_panels]{optimise_panels()}}.
\item Check representation of observed data with \code{\link[=fit_pathway]{fit_pathway()}}.
}

Outputs are local and conditional on the supplied biochemical graph,
grouping of edges into effective rate classes, entry and secretion model,
observation mapping, operating point, and error assumptions.
}
